# A `@widget:` block given where a blueprint whose row has more families is wanted (`@a
# emit Net.* | r`) takes that row as its scope: its lines may emit `Net.*`, which the
# function consumes, though the enclosing widget emits `Ui.*` only (Type System ch. 4,
# "`emit` names a row": only a blueprint with no wanted type emits its scope's row).
# Found by the p14 run on chess (test_worlds' `@OneWire @widget:`).
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*

@Talker: @unit emit Ui.* | Net.*
@Talker:
    Ui.Label($text=$"talks")

@Offline: fn prompt @a emit Net.* | r -> @a emit r
fn @Offline @guest:
    ((result, $tree)) <- @Host @guest, \|path, element| match element:
        Net.Link(..): @ never
        Net.Listen(..): @ never
        Net.Channel(..): @ never
        otherwise: @Element element
    @ result

@page: @unit emit Ui.*
@page:
    @Offline @widget:
        @Talker
        @Talker
